  "as_of_notes": "Report dated 06/01/2026 ('All Voters by County & Party'), the latest monthly Nevada SOS report as of 2026-06-14. Nevada compiles registration statistics on the first business day of each month from the Statewide Voter Registration Database; this is the report covering through end of May 2026. 'Total Voter Registration' here reflects ALL registered voters eligible to vote by the next federal election, including active, inactive, and P-17 (pre-registered 17-year-old) statuses.",
  "data_quality": "high - official Nevada Secretary of State PDF; all 17 county-unit rows captured; every county row sum and all six party column sums independently verified to equal the reported statewide totals (Dem 669,779 + Rep 658,601 + Nonpartisan 964,572 + IndependentAmerican 103,402 + Libertarian 18,180 + Other 40,847 = 2,455,381).",
  "notes": "Nevada has 16 counties plus the independent city of Carson City (FIPS 32510), for 17 county-level units total - all included. Party categories follow the official report columns: Democratic, Republican, Independent American Party, Libertarian, Non-partisan, and Other (a compilation of minor parties). 'Nonpartisan' is Nevada's term for unaffiliated/no-party voters and is the plurality. statewide_total_registered (2,455,381) is ALL registered voters from the 'All Voters by County & Party' sheet. For reference, the same 06/01/2026 reporting cycle lists 2,071,514 ACTIVE registered voters statewide (active by party: Democratic 574,128; Republican 577,737; Independent American 85,682; Libertarian 14,099; Non-Partisan 787,873; Other 31,995), matching the SOS May 2026 news release. The county/party breakdown above is the all-statuses total count. Source page returns HTTP 403 to automated clients; data was retrieved from the official SOS PDFs (document IDs 19369 'All Voters by County & Party' and 19373 'Active Voters by Age & Party', both dated 06/01/2026) via the Internet Archive capture of nvsos.gov. Direct doc URL: https://www.nvsos.gov/home/showpublisheddocument/19369"
